{"from": "claim:ac-07-58-saul-witnesses", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:stephen"}
{"from": "claim:ac-07-04-abraham-after-terah", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:genesis-11-32", "note": "Genesis 11:32: Terah lived 205 years - Stephen's 'after his father was dead' does not fit Genesis's chronology (see also Genesis 12:4)."}
{"from": "claim:ac-07-04-abraham-after-terah", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:genesis-12-4", "note": "Genesis 12:4: Abram left Haran at seventy-five, so on Genesis's numbers he left while Terah was still alive; Stephen's order differs."}
{"from": "claim:ac-07-14-seventy-five-souls", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:genesis-46-27", "note": "Genesis 46:27 (Masoretic Text): seventy souls; Acts 7:14 follows the Septuagint's seventy-five (so LXX Exodus 1:5)."}
{"from": "claim:ac-07-16-burial-shechem", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:genesis-23-17-20", "note": "Genesis 23:17-20: Abraham's purchase is the cave of Machpelah at Hebron from Ephron the Hittite, not a tomb at Shechem from the sons of Hamor."}
{"from": "claim:ac-07-16-burial-shechem", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:joshua-24-32", "note": "Joshua 24:32: Joseph's bones are buried at Shechem in the plot Jacob bought from the sons of Hamor - Jacob's purchase, not Abraham's."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-sanhedrin-6-1-4", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-07-58-stoning-outside-city", "grade": "C", "note": "Mishnah Sanhedrin 6:1-4: the condemned 'is taken out to be stoned. The place of stoning was outside the court and a little beyond it', with the witnesses having a set role. Redacted c. 200 CE, it may not describe the 30s CE procedure exactly, and Acts's impromptu mob stoning does not follow the full Mishnaic rite."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-199-sanhedrin", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-07-58-stoning-outside-city", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus, Ant. 20.9.1: in 62 CE Ananus assembled the sanhedrim and delivered James 'to be stoned' - a stoning execution by the Jerusalem authorities a generation later; it attests the practice, not this stoning."}
